# Modelfile.ornith-9b — primary coding model (Ornith 1.5 generation).
#
# Ornith-1.5-9B at Q6_K. This is the new default primary as of v0.4.0,
# replacing Qwen3.8-27B-Instruct. Ornith 1.5 uses hybrid attention
# (full attention on early layers, linear/kv-cache-friendly attention on
# the rest), so the KV cache stays small and the model holds its
# generation rate as context grows instead of collapsing like a dense
# model of the same size. Measured on the reference box (RTX 3060 12 GB,
# 2026-08): ~37.9 gen tok/s @ 8K ctx → ~37.98 @ 64K ctx (0.0 % drop),
# full VRAM, vs the previous qwen3-27b primary at ~4 t/s @ 64K partial
# offload. This is the "fast default" wins on the day-to-day Go/C#/DevOps
# workload; qwen3-27b stays as secondary for the deep 64K+ agentic
# review/refactor path.
#
# This is a MANUAL GGUF drop, not an Ollama library tag. The GGUF must
# be placed in /bulk/models/ first (see docs/04-models.md → "How to add
# a new model"). The Q6_K build is preferred over the stock Q8_0 for the
# daily driver because it fits 12 GB VRAM comfortably at 64K ctx while
# retaining ~98 % of FP16 quality.
#
# Create with (run from the repo root, so the relative path to
# PROMPT.coding.md resolves and the FROM path exists):
#
#   ollama create ornith-9b -f config/ollama/Modelfile.ornith-9b
#
# Reference: docs/04-models.md (Ornith 1.5 generation section).

FROM /bulk/models/Ornith-1.5-9B-Q6_K.gguf

# Ornith 1.5 uses a plain prompt template (no ChatML). The chat template
# is set by the base model; do NOT override it here or thinking/tool
# handling breaks.

SYSTEM """$(cat config/ollama/PROMPT.coding.md)"""

# Sampling — conservative for code. Lower temperature = more deterministic.
PARAMETER temperature        0.2
PARAMETER top_p              0.95
PARAMETER top_k              40
PARAMETER repeat_penalty     1.05

# Context. 64K is the floor the box runs at for agentic work (Hermes
# Agent requires it for tool use). Ornith 1.5's hybrid attention keeps
# the 64K KV cache small enough to stay in VRAM on the 12 GB card, which
# is exactly why this model does not show the context cliff.
PARAMETER num_ctx            65536

# `keep_alive` is no longer a valid Modelfile PARAMETER in Ollama 0.32.x.
# Server-side default is set in /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service.d/override.conf
# via OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=10m.
